# These run on Linux. On Windows with core.autocrlf=true a checkout rewrites them
# to CRLF, and a commit from that machine can put CRLF into the index. The
# interpreter then reads "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r" and fails with `bad interpreter:
# ...^M` — or, for a Dockerfile entrypoint, `not found` for a file that is plainly
# there. Neither message mentions line endings.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Read by containers, CI and tooling; keep them byte-stable across platforms.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
